{"metadata":{"abstractText":"Hydroxylamine and hydroxamic acid derivatives of a known nonsteroidal antiinflammatory dibenzoxepine series display both cyclooxygenase (CO) and 5-lipoxygenase (5-LO) inhibitory properties. Many of these new dual CO/5-LO inhibitors also exhibit potent topical antiinflammatory activity in the arachidonic acid-induced murine ear edema model. On the basis of their promising profile of in vitro and in vivo activities, hydroxamic acids 24h, 3-(6,11-dihydro-11-oxodibenz[b,e]oxepin-2-yl)-N-hydroxy-N-++ +methylpropanamide (HP 977), and 25, 3-(6,11-dihydrodibenz[b,e]oxepin-2-yl)-N-hydroxy-N- methylpropanamide (P10294), were selected as developmental candidates for the topical treatment of inflammatory skin disorders.","affiliation":"Hoechst-Roussel Pharmaceuticals Inc., Somerville, New Jersey 08876, USA.","authMan":"N","authorList":{"author":[{"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Hoechst-Roussel Pharmaceuticals Inc., Somerville, New Jersey 08876, USA."}]},"firstName":"R R","fullName":"Hamer RR","initials":"RR","lastName":"Hamer"},{"firstName":"J J","fullName":"Tegeler JJ","initials":"JJ","lastName":"Tegeler"},{"firstName":"E S","fullName":"Kurtz ES","initials":"ES","lastName":"Kurtz"},{"firstName":"R C","fullName":"Allen RC","initials":"RC","lastName":"Allen"},{"firstName":"S C","fullName":"Bailey SC","initials":"SC","lastName":"Bailey"},{"firstName":"M E","fullName":"Elliott ME","initials":"ME","lastName":"Elliott"},{"firstName":"L","fullName":"Hellyer L","initials":"L","lastName":"Hellyer"},{"firstName":"G C","fullName":"Helsley GC","initials":"GC","lastName":"Helsley"},{"firstName":"P","fullName":"Przekop P","initials":"P","lastName":"Przekop"},{"firstName":"B S","fullName":"Freed BS","initials":"BS","lastName":"Freed"},{"firstName":"J","fullName":"White J","initials":"J","lastName":"White"},{"firstName":"L L","fullName":"Martin LL","initials":"LL","lastName":"Martin"}]},"authorString":"Hamer RR, Tegeler JJ, Kur